# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live configuration holds the Opensolr API key, the beacon HMAC secret,
# the panel password hash and the IP-anonymisation salt. Only the example file
# belongs in version control.
config/loghound.php
config/*.php
!config/loghound.example.php

# TLS material install.sh generates for a self-signed setup, and any certificate
# or key an operator drops next to the config. A private key in a public repo is
# the fastest way to lose a domain.
config/*.key
config/*.crt
config/*.pem
config/*.cer

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state. Machine-specific, often large, and full of visitor data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# var/ holds the SQLite state database (tail offsets, open sessions, staged
# beacon payloads, geo/ASN caches), PHP sessions, and sampled unparseable log
# lines. All of it is per-install and some of it is personal data.
var/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Logs of any kind, including the badline sample, which contains raw request
# data captured from real traffic.
*.log
logs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
tools/panel-preview-config.php
/tmp/
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies that are deliberately NOT used by this project
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loghound has no Composer or npm dependencies on purpose — `git clone` plus
# install.sh must work on a bare box. These entries exist so that a stray local
# experiment cannot accidentally be committed and imply otherwise.
vendor/
node_modules/
composer.lock
package-lock.json
